# ASDD project steering

**Source of truth:** `.harness/steering/` — parent and every ASDD subagent must **`Read`** these files directly (no `.kiro/steering`).

Index: `.harness/steering/README.md` · Skills: `.harness/steering/skills.md` · Portability: `docs/asdd-harness-portability.md` · Modules: `.agents/modules/README.md`

## When to load steering

**INIT:** Read `.harness/PROGRESS.md` → global `.harness/state/manifest.json` → `.harness/state/slices/<slice-id>/manifest.json` → `paths.features` (if set) → `.harness/steering/` (`structure`, `product`, `manifest`, `codegraph`, `session-loop`). Pick one feature **only** when `phase` is `implementation`. If every slice is `DONE`/`PARKED`/`ABANDONED` and the human named no slice: stop — ask for new intent or explicit unpark.

| Work | Read (minimum) |
|------|----------------|
| Any ASDD work | `structure.md`, `product.md`, `manifest.md`, `codegraph.md`, `session-loop.md` |
| Spec, validation | + `quality-gates.md` (+ `quality-gates.project.md` when judging gates); HTTP/API → skill `api-and-interface-design` if installed |
| Design, tasks, implementation | + `tech.md`, `domain-layer.md` + `domain-layer.project.md`; UI → `design-system.md` if present + frontend skill if installed |
| QA, refactor | + both quality-gates files, domain-layer + binding |
| Domain | + `domain-layer.md` + `domain-layer.project.md` |

## Conventions

- Domain language path from `structure.md` — do not invent entities.
- Business logic: portable `domain-layer.md` + `domain-layer.project.md` (run the binding's gate).
- Specs: EARS; traceability to `capability.md`.
- API/UI conventions from project bindings and enabled modules — never hardcode another product's stack.
- Codegraph first (`codegraph_explore`).
- Quality: CCS ≥ 0.65; see `quality-gates.md` + `.project.md`.

## State

Write `.harness/state/slices/<slice-id>/manifest.json` at end of phase; sync global registry row. Implementation follows `session-loop.md`.
